<!--
The firewalld zone dicerd binds each network's bridge to, while the network
is in use. As libvirt's zone does, it lets guests' traffic be forwarded -
dicerd's own rules decide where to - and lets guests reach the host itself
only for DNS, which dicerd answers on each network's gateway, and ICMP. The
lowest-priority rule turns every other connection to the host away.

To let guests reach another service on the host, as host.dicer.internal,
add it to this zone, which no other interface is in, with firewall-cmd's
add-service or add-port options, as the networking documentation shows.
(An XML comment cannot hold the options themselves: their double hyphen
ends it.)
-->
<zone target="ACCEPT">
  <short>dicer</short>
  <description>The bridges of Dicer's networks. Guests may reach the host for DNS and ICMP only; their other traffic is forwarded as dicerd's rules allow.</description>
  <service name="dns"/>
  <protocol value="icmp"/>
  <rule priority="32767">
    <reject/>
  </rule>
</zone>
